\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Gauge fields, charges and sampling in lattice chirality}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{How does the index of the overlap operator of the
[Wilson kernel](fdip-0153) depend on the connection, in particular for links that
commute, and which integers of the links do the fluxes of closed plaquette surfaces give?
When several species carry
charges, which condition on the charges keeps the coefficient functional fixed by a
cyclic rotation? When the symbol of an operator is sampled on a grid, when do only the
vertices enter the balance of degrees of \ref{fdip-0140}, and which integer replaces that
balance for a Hermitian symbol of any size on a grid of dimension #{n\ge2}? When #{n\ge3},
how does cancellation around singular vertices compare with its counterpart for plaquette fluxes in
\ref{fdip-015X}?}

\p{The first section concerns the Wilson operator with #{c_W=a/2}, any Hermitian
Clifford module with a spin grading, any nonzero finite-dimensional fiber and any unitary connection, unless a
statement names a restriction. The second concerns finite sums of species over a field with
#{2\ne0}, and the third symbols on the momentum grid.}
\transclude{fdip-0151}
\transclude{fdip-015A}
\transclude{fdip-015G}
